# File: autobrr-irc-anti-flap.env.example
# Project role: Shell-compatible dotenv configuration sourced by autobrr-irc-anti-flap.sh.
# Input structure: one KEY=VALUE entry per line; quote shell-sensitive values. The installed copy should
# be /etc/autobrr-irc-anti-flap.env with mode 0600 because it contains the API token.
# Outputs: exported variables consumed by the watchdog; this file has no independent side effects.
# Configuration inputs:
# - AUTOBRR_URL: HTTP base URL string without a required trailing slash; api_get uses it.
# - AUTOBRR_API_TOKEN: secret string sent in X-API-Token by api_get.
# - AUTOBRR_CONTAINER: Docker container name or ID used by all Docker inspection/start/stop functions.
# - STATE_FILE: absolute writable file path used by load_state and save_state.
# - LOCK_FILE: absolute writable file path used by main with flock.
# - POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS: positive integer polling interval used by main.
# - HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: positive integer maximum duration of each API request used by api_get.
# - COOLDOWN_SECONDS: positive integer full cooldown created by begin_cooldown at every detected stop.
# - FAILURE_CONFIRMATIONS: positive integer consecutive qualifying observations required by evaluate_running.
# - FAILURE_WINDOW_SECONDS: positive integer maximum span containing those confirmations.
# - BAD_NETWORK_MINIMUM: positive integer absolute bad-enabled-network threshold.
# - BAD_NETWORK_PERCENT: integer 1..100 percentage threshold; both bad-network thresholds must be met.

AUTOBRR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7474
AUTOBRR_API_TOKEN=replace-with-real-token
AUTOBRR_CONTAINER=autobrr
STATE_FILE=/var/lib/autobrr-irc-anti-flap/state.env
LOCK_FILE=/run/autobrr-irc-anti-flap.lock
POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30
HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
COOLDOWN_SECONDS=300
FAILURE_CONFIRMATIONS=4
FAILURE_WINDOW_SECONDS=180
BAD_NETWORK_MINIMUM=2
BAD_NETWORK_PERCENT=50
